# Step 0 probe catalog (Mygratr)

Each line is a probe or a scar that caught a real failure. When a brief touches
the surface, the matching probe is mandatory in Step 0. Jake runs the probe and
pastes results back. You never fabricate a result.

## The hard rule: never fabricate a CE site fact
Every claim about the CE site (image quality, doc counts, field presence, what a
page renders) must be grounded in LIVE data, not inferred from context files. A
fabricated image-quality figure was caught by self-audit before it shipped to
Claude Code. Probe, do not infer.

## Context files lag reality
Project knowledge files consistently fall behind actual execution state. Verify
currency before trusting any single file. Multi-factor verification before
trusting one document. Prefer catching errors before they propagate into
permanent docs.

## Field maps and live APIs disagree (recurring scar)
The Webflow-to-Sanity field map and the live API have diverged multiple times
(CONTENT-1B, 1C). ALWAYS run a live field-slug sweep against the real source
before writing a migration brief. The field map is a starting point, not truth.
The CONTENT-1E selector scar: Webflow RichText returns
`<div data-rt-embed-type='true'>` (single-quote), NOT the `w-embed` CSS class,
which only exists on the published site. Wrong selector wasted a diagnosis cycle.

## Sanity (the live backend)
- Project `lzbhll1u`, dataset `production`. Studio at
  mygratr-cloudemployee.sanity.studio.
- SCHEMA.md is authoritative over assumptions, but probe the live dataset before
  referencing a field or count. `migrations.status = content_complete`; DESIGN-1
  and TEMPLATE-* do NOT transition state (transitions resume at QA-1 / LAUNCH).
- Image source shape: standard Sanity image object (asset/alt/hotspot/crop).
  Templates pass `source={doc.field}` to E1 Image; never construct URLs by hand.
- Migrator field-write pattern: conditional spread, never null literals.
  `uploadImage()` returns null on empty Webflow source; writing the null literal
  (not omitting it) was the CONTENT-1D-CLEANUP root cause. New migrators must use
  conditional spread (CONVENTIONS.md).

## Components / design (current phase)
- Components separate STRUCTURE (React, locked) from SKIN (tokens). Most
  components re-skin via token swap; a few need shape edits; very few are new.
  Before editing, diff the new Figma component against the existing primitive in
  COMPONENTS.md and tag it re-skin / shape-edit / new.
- Token re-extract (D2) replaces the old teal `#1c787c` era tokens with the new
  Figma's. Probe Storybook after the swap to see which primitives break.
- TEMPLATE-BLOG is the pattern template. All other detail templates inherit its
  route + GROQ/Zod + JSON-LD + B3 PortableText patterns. Read it before building
  a new template.

## Routes / build
- File-path collision check before adding a route or component.
- Next.js 16.2.4, Tailwind v4, app router. Vercel root directory override is
  `site/`. Locales: US default + `/uk/` prefix.
- "Built != working." Tests do not prove correctness. Visual eyeball checks at
  named HALTs have caught real errors automated gates missed. Prod/staging smoke
  is part of the phase.

## Don't-touch / intentional list
- `migrations.status` stays `content_complete` through all design + template
  phases. Do not transition it.
- The raw CONTENT-1E embed recovery (142 tables + 7 videoEmbeds) is canonical. Do
  not re-flatten or re-run the old htmlToBlocks path.
- DESIGN-1 Brief B Steps 7, 9, 10, 11 are parked deliberately. Do not "finish"
  them mid-phase unless the active brief calls for it.
